The port's expected output for the singlenode suite, where it differs from
the expected output of PostgreSQL 19 or of Cloudberry for a reason of the
port's own.  Each file is here for the reason below, and cloudberry.md,
"The singlenode suites", gives the reasons in full.

A file named test_9.out is an alternative for one of PostgreSQL's tests,
which pg_regress accepts as well as PostgreSQL's own; a file named test.out
replaces Cloudberry's expected output for one of Cloudberry's, or is the
expected output of one of the port's own, in ../sql.

gp_setup.out
    The port's setup, run after PostgreSQL's tests and before Cloudberry's:
    it creates the extensions of every M1 module, whose SQL objects
    Cloudberry's tests use and Cloudberry has built in.

security_label_9.out
    PostgreSQL's test runs its unqualified SECURITY LABEL statements where
    no label provider is loaded, and expects "no security label providers
    have been loaded".  The port's modules register three -- gp, gp_tag and
    gp_profile -- so the same statements are refused with "must specify
    provider when multiple security label providers have been loaded".
    Six lines, each that message; nothing else differs.
